                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A political philosophy that focuses on human rights."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "derogatory",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b0ae29d6-3fb8-4ea3-84b3-5f557320d15e",
                                                "sense_id": "0dc9a80d-dbd0-3950-9487-b9634919d409",
                                                "text": "With the notion of human-rightism, Pellet (2000) tried to warn of the costs and dangers of the slippery slope of activism within the arena of international human rights law. ‘Human-rightism’ was immediately ascribed pejorative meanings and used to express different forms of critique when it came to human rights."
                                            }
